00:16:55,248 --> 00:16:58,545
Your assignment has four questions. One:

194
00:16:58,565 --> 00:17:02,278
a 2500-line encoder with times-four decoding.

195
00:17:02,298 --> 00:17:08,581
Find the speed-measurement error of the M method and the T method at 150 and

196
00:17:08,601 --> 00:17:09,742
at 3000 r/min,

197
00:17:09,762 --> 00:17:15,962
and say which belongs in needle positioning and which in high-speed sewing.

198
00:17:15,982 --> 00:17:19,528
The M method counts pulses in a fixed time;

199
00:17:19,548 --> 00:17:24,836
the T method times the gap between two pulses with a fast clock.

200
00:17:25,236 --> 00:17:30,301
Two: with today's trimming solenoid and a trimming speed of 450 r/min,

201
00:17:30,321 --> 00:17:34,442
does each freewheeling scheme meet the limit? Choose one,

202
00:17:34,462 --> 00:17:40,035
and give the transistor's voltage rating and the energy the Zener absorbs per

203
00:17:40,055 --> 00:17:40,616
release.

204
00:17:41,016 --> 00:17:45,574
Three: the shaft makes an emergency stop from 4500 r/min.

205
00:17:45,594 --> 00:17:50,553
Without a braking resistor, how high does the link voltage go,

206
00:17:50,573 --> 00:17:55,854
and above what speed is the resistor needed? Four is a discussion:

207
00:17:55,874 --> 00:17:59,950
should an electronic feed use a stepper or a servo?

208
00:17:59,970 --> 00:18:05,973
A stepper moves one step per pulse, but can lose steps under too much load.

209
00:18:05,993 --> 00:18:11,996
Compare positioning, the risk of lost steps, low-speed smoothness and cost.

