219
00:18:57,246 --> 00:18:58,820
Three things to remember.

220
00:18:59,220 --> 00:19:04,528
One: the shaft servo nests current, velocity and position loops;

221
00:19:04,548 --> 00:19:10,772
needle positioning slows down first and then switches to the position loop,

222
00:19:10,792 --> 00:19:15,600
with a position gain of a quarter to a half of K_v over J,

223
00:19:15,620 --> 00:19:18,680
retuned whenever the inertia changes.

224
00:19:19,080 --> 00:19:24,457
Two: without a velocity-loop integral,

225
00:19:24,477 --> 00:19:31,701
friction leaves a steady error of T_f over K_v K_p.

226
00:19:32,101 --> 00:19:36,634
Three: solenoids use a boost plus chopped hold,

227
00:19:36,654 --> 00:19:39,928
Zener freewheeling speeds release,

228
00:19:39,948 --> 00:19:45,353
and delays convert to shaft angle by theta equals 6 n t,

229
00:19:45,373 --> 00:19:48,841
which sets the trimming-speed limit.

